Complete Docker + Flask Beginner Guide

This document covers:
1.	Install Docker
2.	Create Docker User Permission
3.	Fix Docker Permission Issues
4.	Create Flask Application
5.	Create Dockerfile
6.	Build Docker Image
7.	Run Docker Container
8.	Push Image to Docker Hub
9.	Delete Docker Images/Containers
________________________________________

1. Install Docker (Ubuntu/Linux)
Update packages:
sudo apt update
Install Docker:
sudo apt install docker.io -y
Check Docker version:
docker --version
Start Docker service:
sudo systemctl start docker
Enable Docker service:
sudo systemctl enable docker
Check Docker status:
sudo systemctl status docker
________________________________________

2. Create Docker User Permission
By default Docker needs sudo access.
To allow normal user to run Docker commands:
Add current user to Docker group:
sudo usermod -aG docker $USER
Apply changes:
newgrp docker
OR logout/login again.
Check groups:
groups
You should see:
docker
Now test:
docker ps
________________________________________

3. Fix Docker Permission Error
If you still get:
permission denied while trying to connect to the docker API
Run:
sudo chmod 666 /var/run/docker.sock
Restart Docker:
sudo systemctl restart docker
Test:
docker ps
________________________________________

4. Create Flask Application
Create project folder:
mkdir flask-app
cd flask-app
Create Python file:
nano app.py
Add this code:
from flask import Flask

app = Flask(__name__)

@app.route("/")
def home():
    return "Hello from Flask Docker App"

app.run(host="0.0.0.0", port=5000)
Save file.
________________________________________

5. Create Dockerfile

Vim Dockerfile
FROM python:3.11

WORKDIR /app

COPY . .

RUN pip install flask

EXPOSE 5000

CMD ["python", "app.py"]
Save file.
________________________________________
6. Project Structure
flask-app/
 ├── app.py
 ├── Dockerfile
________________________________________
7. Build Docker Image
Build image:
docker build -t flask-app .
Check images:
docker images
________________________________________

8. Run Docker Container
Run container:
docker run -d -p 5000:5000 flask-app
Check running containers:
docker ps
Open browser:
http://localhost:5000
You should see:
Hello from Flask Docker App
________________________________________

9. Docker Commands
Check running containers:
docker ps
Check all containers:
docker ps -a
Check images:
docker images
Stop container:
docker stop <container_id>
Remove container:
docker rm <container_id>
Delete image:
docker rmi flask-app
Force delete image:
docker rmi -f flask-app
Delete all images:
docker rmi $(docker images -q)
________________________________________

10. Create Docker Hub Account
Go to Docker Hub:
https://hub.docker.com
Create account.
________________________________________

11. Login to Docker Hub
Run:
docker login
Enter:
•	Docker Hub username
•	Password
________________________________________
12. Tag Docker Image
Docker Hub image format:
username/image-name:tag
Example:
docker tag flask-app palashdevops/flask-app:latest
Check images:
docker images
________________________________________

13. Push Image to Docker Hub
Run:
docker push palashdevops/flask-app:latest
Image will upload to Docker Hub.
________________________________________

14. Pull Image from Docker Hub
Run:
docker pull palashdevops/flask-app:latest
________________________________________

15. Run Pulled Image
Run:
docker run -d -p 5000:5000 palashdevops/flask-app:latest
________________________________________

